  "lines": [
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "I got a message from my bank saying my account is locked. It looked totally real. Could it be a scam?",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "mail",
          "label": "MESSAGE"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "warn",
          "label": "SCAM?"
        },
        "subtitle": "AI scams, simple checks",
        "mid": "VS"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "It could be. Scammers now use AI to write messages, copy voices, and even fake videos. But a few simple habits beat most of them.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "shield",
        "text": "Simple habits win",
        "cue": "habits"
      },
      "punch": "habits"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So what will we cover?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "How AI changed scams, the red flags to watch for, voice and video tricks, a safe-check habit, and what to do if you already clicked.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "TODAY",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "How scams changed",
            "icon": "robot",
            "cue": "changed"
          },
          {
            "label": "Red flags",
            "icon": "warn",
            "cue": "red"
          },
          {
            "label": "Voice & video tricks",
            "icon": "phone",
            "cue": "voice"
          },
          {
            "label": "Safe-check habit",
            "icon": "check",
            "cue": "safe-check"
          },
          {
            "label": "If you clicked",
            "icon": "shield",
            "cue": "clicked"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "First, what is phishing, exactly?",
      "chapter": "Why scams got smarter",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🎣",
        "text": "Phishing?",
        "cue": "phishing"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Phishing is when someone pretends to be a company or person you trust, to trick you into giving away passwords, codes, or money.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "HOW PHISHING WORKS",
        "traveler": "🎣",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🎭",
            "label": "Pretends to be trusted",
            "cue": "pretends"
          },
          {
            "icon": "💬",
            "label": "Tricks you",
            "cue": "trick"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🔑",
            "label": "Takes passwords or money",
            "cue": "passwords"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#FF4D6D"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "I thought scam messages were full of spelling mistakes.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "x",
        "text": "Spelling mistakes?",
        "cue": "spelling"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "They used to be. Now AI can write perfect, friendly messages in many languages, so good spelling is no longer a sign it's safe.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "OLD SCAMS",
          "color": "#0A84FF",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Spelling mistakes",
              "icon": "x",
              "cue": "used"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "AI SCAMS",
          "color": "#E91E63",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Perfect & friendly",
              "icon": "warn",
              "cue": "perfect"
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "What else can AI do for them?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "It can make messages personal, using details from your public posts, like your job, your pet's name, or a recent trip.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "PUBLIC CLUES",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Your job",
            "icon": "suitcase",
            "cue": "job"
          },
          {
            "label": "Your pet's name",
            "icon": "🐶",
            "cue": "pet"
          },
          {
            "label": "A recent trip",
            "icon": "globe",
            "cue": "trip"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#8E44AD"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "That's creepy."
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "It is. So a message that knows things about you isn't proof it's real. And think about what you share publicly.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "lock",
        "text": "Knows you ≠ real",
        "cue": "knows",
        "sub": "Share less publicly",
        "sub_cue": "share"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So how do I spot a scam if it looks perfect?",
      "chapter": "Red flags",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "search",
        "text": "Spot the red flags",
        "cue": "spot"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Look at how the message wants you to feel. Scams love pressure. Act now, your account is locked, you won a prize.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Pressure flags",
        "icon": "warn",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Act now!",
            "cue": "act",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Account locked!",
            "cue": "locked",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "You won a prize!",
            "cue": "prize",
            "ok": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Why pressure?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Because when we panic or get excited, we stop thinking carefully. Scammers want you to rush.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "⏱️",
        "text": "Rushing = risk",
        "cue": "rush"
      },
      "punch": "rush"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "What else should I watch for?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "What they ask for. Your password, a one-time code, your card details, or payment by gift card or crypto.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "They ask for",
        "icon": "lock",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Password",
            "cue": "password",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "One-time code",
            "cue": "one-time",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Card details",
            "cue": "card",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Gift cards or crypto",
            "cue": "gift",
            "ok": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And links?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Be careful with links. A web address can look almost right but be slightly off, like an extra letter or a strange ending.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔗",
        "text": "Almost-right links",
        "cue": "links",
        "sub": "One letter off",
        "sub_cue": "letter"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "So here's the rule. Real banks and companies won't ask for your password or one-time code by message or phone.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "They won't ask for",
        "icon": "shield",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Your password",
            "cue": "password",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Your one-time code",
            "cue": "one-time",
            "ok": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "You mentioned voices. Can AI really copy someone's voice?",
      "chapter": "Voice and video tricks",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "user",
          "label": "REAL"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "robot",
          "label": "COPY"
        },
        "subtitle": "Voice clones",
        "mid": "VS"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes. From a short recording, AI can make a voice that sounds like someone you know. Scammers may call pretending family is in trouble.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "VOICE CLONE SCAM",
        "traveler": "📞",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "🎙️",
            "label": "Short recording",
            "cue": "recording"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🤖",
            "label": "AI copies the voice",
            "cue": "sounds"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🆘",
            "label": "Fake emergency",
            "cue": "trouble"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#FF4D6D"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "That's scary. What do I do if I get a call like that?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Hang up, and call the person back on the number you already have. A real family member won't mind.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "SUSPICIOUS CALL",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Hang up",
            "icon": "x",
            "cue": "hang"
          },
          {
            "label": "Call back yourself",
            "icon": "phone",
            "cue": "call"
          },
          {
            "label": "Use the number you have",
            "icon": "check",
            "cue": "number"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Some families also pick a secret code word that only they know. If the caller can't say it, that's a big warning sign.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🔐",
        "text": "Family code word",
        "cue": "code",
        "sub": "No word? Warning!",
        "sub_cue": "warning"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "I like that. Let's pick ours tonight, at dinner, not online.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🍽️",
        "text": "Pick it in person",
        "cue": "dinner"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "And videos can be faked too. If a video call feels off, or someone famous promises you money, be extra careful.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Video red flags",
        "icon": "eye",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Something feels off",
            "cue": "off",
            "ok": false
          },
          {
            "text": "Famous person + money",
            "cue": "famous",
            "ok": false
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Okay. So what's the one habit that protects me?",
      "chapter": "The safe-check habit",
      "board": {
        "type": "title",
        "left": {
          "icon": "warn",
          "label": "PANIC"
        },
        "right": {
          "icon": "check",
          "label": "PAUSE"
        },
        "subtitle": "The safe-check habit",
        "mid": "→"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Pause. Don't click, don't reply. Then open the official app or website yourself, and check there.",
      "board": {
        "type": "journey",
        "title": "SAFE CHECK",
        "traveler": "📩",
        "items": [
          {
            "icon": "⏸️",
            "label": "Pause",
            "cue": "pause"
          },
          {
            "icon": "🚫",
            "label": "Don't click",
            "cue": "don't"
          },
          {
            "icon": "📱",
            "label": "Official app",
            "cue": "official"
          },
          {
            "icon": "✅",
            "label": "Check there",
            "cue": "check"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      },
      "punch": "pause"
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Why not just tap the link to check?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Because the link might lead to a fake page that looks just like the real one. Typing the address yourself, or using the app, is safer.",
      "board": {
        "type": "compare",
        "left": {
          "label": "TAP THE LINK",
          "color": "#FF4D6D",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Might be fake",
              "icon": "x",
              "cue": "fake"
            }
          ]
        },
        "right": {
          "label": "GO YOURSELF",
          "color": "#2ECC71",
          "items": [
            {
              "text": "Type it or use the app",
              "icon": "check",
              "cue": "typing",
              "tick": true
            }
          ]
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And if someone calls saying they're from my bank?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Hang up and call the number on the back of your card. Real banks will never be upset that you checked.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "phone",
        "text": "Number on your card",
        "cue": "card",
        "sub": "Real banks won't mind",
        "sub_cue": "real"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Also turn on two-step verification for important accounts. Then a stolen password alone isn't enough to get in.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Extra shield",
        "icon": "shield",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Two-step verification",
            "cue": "two-step",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Stolen password not enough",
            "cue": "stolen",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Anything else?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Use a different password for each important account, and keep your phone and apps updated. A password manager can help.",
      "board": {
        "type": "checklist",
        "title": "Everyday shields",
        "icon": "lock",
        "items": [
          {
            "text": "Different passwords",
            "cue": "different",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Keep apps updated",
            "cue": "updated",
            "ok": true
          },
          {
            "text": "Password manager",
            "cue": "manager",
            "ok": true
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Okay, but what if I already clicked? Or typed my password?",
      "chapter": "If you clicked",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "warn",
        "text": "Already clicked?",
        "cue": "clicked"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Don't panic, and don't feel embarrassed. It happens to smart people. Just act fast.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "💙",
        "text": "It happens. Act fast.",
        "cue": "act"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Change that password right away, and anywhere else you used it. If money or cards are involved, call your bank on the official number.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "IF YOU CLICKED",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Change the password",
            "icon": "lock",
            "cue": "change"
          },
          {
            "label": "Change it everywhere",
            "icon": "🔁",
            "cue": "anywhere"
          },
          {
            "label": "Call your bank",
            "icon": "phone",
            "cue": "call"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#0A84FF"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Should I tell anyone?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes. Report the message in the app or email service, and tell your family. Warning others helps stop scams spreading.",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "THEN",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Report it",
            "icon": "shield",
            "cue": "report"
          },
          {
            "label": "Tell family",
            "icon": "user",
            "cue": "tell"
          },
          {
            "label": "Warn others",
            "icon": "mail",
            "cue": "warning"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "And for kids or grandparents?"
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Talk about it often. Agree that anyone can ask, is this real, without feeling silly. Asking first is always okay.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "user",
        "text": "Asking is always okay",
        "cue": "asking"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Quiz time, Dad! A message has perfect spelling and knows your name. Is it safe? Think...",
      "chapter": "Quiz",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "❓",
        "text": "Quiz time!",
        "cue": "quiz",
        "sub": "Perfect spelling = safe?",
        "sub_cue": "perfect"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Not necessarily! AI writes perfect messages now. I still check it myself.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "x",
        "text": "Still check!",
        "cue": "check"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Right! Next. Your bank calls and asks for your one-time code. What do you do? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "📞",
        "text": "Bank wants your code?",
        "cue": "code"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Never share it. Hang up, and call the number on my card.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "check",
        "text": "Hang up, call back",
        "cue": "hang"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Yes! Last one. A family member calls in trouble, needing money fast. What's your move? Think...",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "🆘",
        "text": "Urgent family call?",
        "cue": "family"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "Hang up, call them back on their usual number, and ask for our code word!",
      "board": {
        "type": "steps",
        "title": "MY MOVE",
        "items": [
          {
            "label": "Hang up",
            "icon": "x",
            "cue": "hang"
          },
          {
            "label": "Call back",
            "icon": "phone",
            "cue": "call"
          },
          {
            "label": "Ask the code word",
            "icon": "🔐",
            "cue": "code"
          }
        ],
        "color": "#2ECC71"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "DAD",
      "text": "So: pressure is a warning sign, check it yourself, and never share codes.",
      "board": {
        "type": "summary",
        "rows": [
          {
            "text": "PRESSURE = WARNING",
            "icon": "warn",
            "cue": "pressure",
            "color": "#0A84FF"
          },
          {
            "text": "CHECK IT YOURSELF",
            "icon": "search",
            "cue": "check",
            "color": "#E91E63"
          },
          {
            "text": "NEVER SHARE CODES",
            "icon": "lock",
            "cue": "never",
            "color": "#2ECC71"
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "Perfect score! And if something slips through, act fast and report it. No shame, just action.",
      "board": {
        "type": "big",
        "icon": "shield",
        "text": "Act fast, report it",
        "cue": "act"
      }
    },
    {
      "who": "TEEN",
      "text": "You got it! Subscribe to AI Nation Studio, and share this with a friend! And next time a message says act now... will you pause and check?"
    }
  ]
}